SYSTEM BREAK1:INTENTIONALLY STOPPED DOWNSTREAM SERVICES TO CHECK SYSTEM BEHAVIOUR -> RESULT 500 INTERNAL SERVER ERROR
BUT HERE EVERY REQUEST HITS DOWNSTREAM SERVICES EVEN THOUGH CONSTANTLY MORE THAN 50% REQUESTS ARE FACING SERVERDOWN ERROR WHICH RESULTS IN SLOW SYSTEM
THERE COMES A RESLIENCE PATTERN CALLED "CIRCUIT BREAKER"

CIRCUIT BREAKER working
Step 1: Monitor last 10 calls
Step 2: If 5 or more fail → OPEN circuit
Step 3: Stop calling service for 10 sec goes to fallback
Step 4: After 10 sec → try again


SYSTEM BREAK2: MADE PAYMENT SERVICE SLEEP FOR 8SECS RESULTING IN HIGH LATENCY SYSTEM
->MADE TIMEDOUT(2SEC) CONFIGURATION IN PAYMENTCLIENT WHICH RESULTS IN EARLY FAILURE RATHER THAN LOW LATENCY BEHAVIOUR


